  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Preprocessing Mental Model and Scaling",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Preprocessing Mental Model and Scaling",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Preprocessing Does",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Turns raw columns into ==numeric== model-ready features",
                "`fit` learns stats (mean, min, median) from data",
                "`transform` applies those learned stats"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Three Scalers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Standard",
                "MinMax",
                "Robust"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Formula",
                  "(x - mean) / std",
                  "(x - min) / (max - min)",
                  "(x - median) / IQR"
                ],
                [
                  "Result",
                  "mean 0, std 1, no fixed range",
                  "==[0, 1]==",
                  "no fixed range"
                ],
                [
                  "Outliers",
                  "sensitive",
                  "one squashes the rest",
                  "{green:resists}"
                ],
                [
                  "Use",
                  "general default",
                  "pixels, neural nets",
                  "outliers present"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Scale}: KNN, SVM, regularised linear/logistic, PCA, neural nets",
                "{red:Skip}: tree models, since splits ignore scale"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example: Fit on Train Only",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "scaler = StandardScaler().fit(X_train)",
                "X_train_s = scaler.transform(X_train)",
                "X_test_s = scaler.transform(X_test)"
              ],
              "note": "test set is only transformed"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never fit on the test set",
              "text": "Fit learns stats, so fitting on test data leaks them and inflates the score."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why not fit on test?** It leaks test stats into training",
                "**Do trees need scaling?** No, splits depend on order only",
                "**Outliers present?** Use RobustScaler (median and IQR)"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Encoding Categorical Features",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Encoding Categorical Features",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pick the Encoder",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:OneHotEncoder}: one 0/1 column per category, for ==nominal== data",
                "`handle_unknown='ignore'` so unseen test categories do not crash",
                "{blue:OrdinalEncoder}: integers in your order, ==only== for truly ordered features"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore')",
                "OrdinalEncoder(categories=[['low','med','high']])",
                "LabelEncoder().fit_transform(y)"
              ],
              "note": "the last one is for the target only"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Encoder",
                "Use on",
                "Never on"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`OneHotEncoder`",
                  "nominal X",
                  "ordered X"
                ],
                [
                  "`OrdinalEncoder`",
                  "ordered X",
                  "nominal X"
                ],
                [
                  "`LabelEncoder`",
                  "target `y`",
                  "input features"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Dummy Trap",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Dummy columns sum to 1, so they are ==perfectly collinear==",
                "`OneHotEncoder(drop='first')` for unregularised linear models",
                "Regularised models and trees can keep every column"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. High Cardinality",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Thousands of levels",
                "How"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "One-hot",
                  "width explodes: avoid"
                ],
                [
                  "`TargetEncoder`",
                  "category mean of y; fit ==inside CV=="
                ],
                [
                  "Frequency",
                  "replace with count or share"
                ],
                [
                  "Hashing",
                  "fixed width, collisions allowed"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "`LabelEncoder` on features invents a fake order. A `TargetEncoder` fitted outside CV ==leaks== the target."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Handling Missing Values",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Handling Missing Values",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Detect and Decide",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`df.isna().sum()` counts ==NaN== per column",
                "{green:MCAR}: missing completely at random, safe to impute",
                "{orange:Informative}: the missingness itself predicts the target"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. SimpleImputer",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "strategy",
                "Use for"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`mean`",
                  "symmetric numerics"
                ],
                [
                  "`median`",
                  "==skewed== numerics"
                ],
                [
                  "`most_frequent`",
                  "categoricals"
                ],
                [
                  "`constant`",
                  "with `fill_value=...`"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "imp = SimpleImputer(strategy='median',",
                "                    add_indicator=True)",
                "X_tr = imp.fit_transform(X_train)",
                "X_te = imp.transform(X_test)"
              ],
              "note": "fit on train only, transform everything else"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Statistics are learned on ==train only==, then reused on val and test",
                "`add_indicator=True` appends a binary **was missing** column",
                "Keeps the signal when missingness is informative"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Model-Based Options",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`KNNImputer`: fills from the ==k nearest== rows",
                "`IterativeImputer`: models each feature from the others",
                "Both are slower; `KNNImputer` is distance-based, so it needs ==scaled== data",
                "`HistGradientBoosting` handles NaN natively"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Split first",
              "text": "Fitting an imputer on all data leaks test statistics. Put it inside a Pipeline."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Feature Selection Methods",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Feature Selection Methods",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Filter, Wrapper, Embedded",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Filter}: score features ==without the model==",
                "`VarianceThreshold` drops near-constant columns",
                "`SelectKBest(f_classif or mutual_info_classif, k=10)` keeps top k",
                "{purple:Wrapper}: `RFE(est, n_features_to_select=k)` refits, drops weakest",
                "{green:Embedded}: `Lasso`/L1 zeroes coefficients",
                "`SelectFromModel(RandomForest)` thresholds `feature_importances_`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Filter",
                "Wrapper",
                "Embedded"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Speed",
                  "**fast**",
                  "{red:slow}",
                  "middle"
                ],
                [
                  "Model",
                  "agnostic",
                  "specific",
                  "specific"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Leak-Proof Selection",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Split",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fit selector",
                    "sub": "train fold only",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Transform",
                    "sub": "train + test",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "x",
                    "text": "Score",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "pipe = Pipeline([('sel', SelectKBest(f_classif, k=10)),",
                "                 ('clf', LogisticRegression())])",
                "cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=5)"
              ],
              "note": "selector refits inside every fold"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Leak",
              "text": "Selecting on the ==full dataset== before CV **inflates** scores."
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Filter vs wrapper?** Filter is fast and model-agnostic; wrapper refits the model, slow.",
                "**How does Lasso select?** L1 zeroes coefficients.",
                "**Why not select before CV?** Test rows leak into selection."
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Data Leakage and Scikit-learn Pipelines",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Data Leakage and Scikit-learn Pipelines",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Leakage Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Leakage==: test-set or future information reaches training",
                "Metric looks {green:optimistic}; production performance {red:collapses}"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Scaler, imputer or selector fitted on ==all data== before the split",
                "Features derived from the **target**",
                "**Duplicate** rows across train and test",
                "Random split on time series: use `TimeSeriesSplit`"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Leak-Proof Pipeline",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`Pipeline.fit(X_train, y_train)` refits ==every step== on the training fold only",
                "So `cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=5)` is **leak-free**",
                "`ColumnTransformer` gives each column group its own preprocessing",
                "Unlisted columns are dropped: `remainder='drop'` is the default"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "ct = ColumnTransformer([",
                "  ('num', num_pipe, num_cols),",
                "  ('cat', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'),",
                "   cat_cols)])",
                "pipe = Pipeline([('prep', ct), ('model', clf)])",
                "cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=5)"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Tune and Ship",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Grid keys use ==step__param== naming: `model__C`",
                "`joblib.dump` the **whole** fitted pipeline so serving repeats the same preprocessing"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "gs = GridSearchCV(pipe, {'model__C': [0.1, 1, 10]})",
                "gs.fit(X_train, y_train)",
                "joblib.dump(gs.best_estimator_, 'pipe.joblib')"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Golden rule",
              "text": "Split first, then fit on train only. Cross-validate the ==whole pipeline==, never pre-transformed data."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Preprocessing Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Preprocessing Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Scale, Encode, Impute",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Step",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Scale",
                  "`StandardScaler` general, `MinMaxScaler` bounded, `RobustScaler` outliers; {green:trees need none}"
                ],
                [
                  "Encode",
                  "`OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore')` nominal, `OrdinalEncoder` ordered, `LabelEncoder` only y"
                ],
                [
                  "Impute",
                  "`SimpleImputer` ==median== numeric, ==most_frequent== categorical; `add_indicator=True` if missingness informative"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Select Features",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Tools"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Filter",
                  "`VarianceThreshold`, then `SelectKBest`"
                ],
                [
                  "Wrapper",
                  "`RFE`"
                ],
                [
                  "Embedded",
                  "`SelectFromModel`, Lasso"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. The Golden Rule",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Split",
                    "sub": "first",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "fit(train)",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "transform",
                    "sub": "train and test",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cross-validate",
                    "sub": "whole pipeline",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "num = make_pipeline(SimpleImputer(strategy='median'), StandardScaler())",
                "pre = ColumnTransformer([('num', num, num_cols),",
                "    ('cat', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore'), cat_cols)])",
                "pipe = Pipeline([('prep', pre), ('model', clf)])",
                "cross_val_score(pipe, X, y, cv=5)"
              ],
              "note": "Pipeline + ColumnTransformer refit every step per fold"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never",
              "text": "Fit scaler, imputer or selector on all data before splitting. It leaks the test set."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Spot the bug: `X_s = StandardScaler().fit_transform(X)` runs first, then `train_test_split(X_s, y)`. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The mean and std were learned from the test rows too, so this is ==leakage==.",
                "Split first, then `fit` on train only. Or put the scaler in a Pipeline."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An encoder is fitted on colours ['red','blue']. What happens when it transforms ['green']?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "A default `OneHotEncoder()` raises `ValueError` for the unknown category.",
                "With `handle_unknown='ignore'` the row becomes all zeros."
              ],
              "example_code": [
                "enc = OneHotEncoder().fit([['red'],['blue']])",
                "enc.transform([['green']])"
              ]
            },
            {
              "q": "You run `SelectKBest` on all of X, then `cross_val_score` on the reduced X. Why is the score too high?",
              "type": "qa",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Selection used the labels of every validation fold, so it is leaky.",
                "Put the selector inside the Pipeline, so each fold refits it on its training part."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
